  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Certification of Community-based Water Technicians</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The increasing unpredictability and poor quality of local water supply for both irrigation and consumption negatively impacts the health and food security of many communities in Honduras and can push people to leave their communities in search of better living conditions in larger cities or across borders. To increase water access and quality for rural families in Honduras the Asociacin Hondurea de Juntas Administradoras de Sistemas de Agua (AHJASA) will train and certify 100 water technicians to provide technical assistance to approximately 300 community-based water system organizations. At the IAF we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Honduras. AHJASA&apos;s activities in training water technicians support local entrepreneurship while ensuring healthy families. This grant is part of the IAF&apos;s efforts to address the root causes of irregular migration in Central America.</narrative>
  </description>
